eb-mar-2025-newsletter-4','','','2025-10-21 13:07:42','2025-10-21 02:07:42','',849,'http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/SHASA-Feb-Mar-2025-newsletter.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),(851,1,'2025-10-21 13:07:44','2025-10-21 02:07:44','<!-- wp:file {\"id\":850,\"href\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/SHASA-Feb-Mar-2025-newsletter.pdf\",\"displayPreview\":true} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-file\"><object class=\"wp-block-file__embed\" data=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/SHASA-Feb-Mar-2025-newsletter.pdf\" type=\"application/pdf\" style=\"width:100%;height:600px\" aria-label=\"SHASA-Feb-Mar-2025-newsletter\"></object><a id=\"wp-block-file--media-5fde0754-202d-4635-badc-44aeeceb32dd\" href=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/SHASA-Feb-Mar-2025-newsletter.pdf\">SHASA-Feb-Mar-2025-newsletter</a><a href=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/SHASA-Feb-Mar-2025-newsletter.pdf\" class=\"wp-block-file__button wp-element-button\" download aria-describedby=\"wp-block-file--media-5fde0754-202d-4635-badc-44aeeceb32dd\">Download</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:file -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Newsletter January 2025','','inherit','closed','closed','','849-revision-v1','','','2025-10-21 13:07:44','2025-10-21 02:07:44','',849,'http://172.19.125.1:8080/?p=851',0,'revision','',0),(852,1,'2025-10-21 13:10:20','2025-10-21 02:10:20','<!-- wp:template-part {\"slug\":\"header\",\"theme\":\"twentytwentyfive\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/banner.png\",\"id\":163,\"dimRatio\":50,\"overlayColor\":\"contrast\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"align\":\"center\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"},\"blockGap\":\"0\",\"margin\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover aligncenter\" style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-top:0;padding-bottom:0\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-163 size-full\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/banner.png\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading {\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"className\":\"is-style-default\",\"fontSize\":\"xx-large\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-left is-style-default has-xx-large-font-size\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-base-color\">Heat Haven</mark>s</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark>Bushfire and Heatwave Havens</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In partnership with community organisations that run facilities, SHASA has undertaken upgrades on seven buildings so far:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Red Door Hall, Anglican Parish (solar, batteries, air conditioning, blinds, insulation, kitchen upgrade)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Moruya PreSchool Kindergarten (solar, batteries, backup generator, pump, fire hoses)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>CWA Moruya (solar, batteries, backup gas generator, air conditioning, HEPA filters, electrical upgrade, LED lighting and window shutters)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>CWA Narooma (new roof, insulation, solar, batteries, new flooring, kitchen upgrade, window shutters)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Uniting Church Catalina (solar, batteries, backup generators, HEPA filters, accessible toilet, washing machine, fridges, shelving, replacement of gas heaters with air conditioners)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Anglican Church Batemans Bay (electrical upgrade, LED lighting, solar, and batteries)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Moruya Surf Club (solar batteries, backup generator, LED lighting, air conditioning and filters)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>SHASA is currently seeking grant funding to upgrade the following buildings:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Southern Life Church Moruya</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Broulee Surf Club</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Anglican Parish Batemans Bay (Stage 3)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>SHASA believes it is time to update the strategy to a Community Resilience Strategy and add facilities that need just solar and batteries to reduce their electricity costs.&nbsp; If you know of a community building that may benefit from SHASA’s assistance, please send an email with details to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact.shasa@gmail.com\">contact.shasa@gmail.com</a>&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:open-user-map/map /--></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:template-part {\"slug\":\"footer\",\"theme\":\"twentytwentyfive\"} /-->','page-heat-havens','','inherit','closed','closed','','697-revision-v1','','','2025-10-21 13:10:20','2025-10-21 02:10:20','',697,'http://172.19.125.1:8080/?p=852',0,'revision','',0),(854,1,'2025-10-21 13:19:14','2025-10-21 02:19:14','<!-- wp:template-part {\"slug\":\"header\",\"theme\":\"twentytwentyfive\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/banner.png\",\"id\":163,\"dimRatio\":50,\"overlayColor\":\"contrast\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"align\":\"center\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"},\"blockGap\":\"0\",\"margin\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover aligncenter\" style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-top:0;padding-bottom:0\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-163 size-full\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/banner.png\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading {\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"className\":\"is-style-default\",\"fontSize\":\"xx-large\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-left is-style-default has-xx-large-font-size\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-base-color\">Heat Haven</mark>s</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-contrast-color\">Bushfire and Heatwave Havens</mark></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In partnership with community organisations that run facilities, SHASA has undertaken upgrades on seven buildings so far:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Red Door Hall, Anglican Parish (solar, batteries, air conditioning, blinds, insulation, kitchen upgrade)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Moruya PreSchool Kindergarten (solar, batteries, backup generator, pump, fire hoses)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>CWA Moruya (solar, batteries, backup gas generator, air conditioning, HEPA filters, electrical upgrade, LED lighting and window shutters)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>CWA Narooma (new roof, insulation, solar, batteries, new flooring, kitchen upgrade, window shutters)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Uniting Church Catalina (solar, batteries, backup generators, HEPA filters, accessible toilet, washing machine, fridges, shelving, replacement of gas heaters with air conditioners)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Anglican Church Batemans Bay (electrical upgrade, LED lighting, solar, and batteries)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Moruya Surf Club (solar batteries, backup generator, LED lighting, air conditioning and filters)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>SHASA is currently seeking grant funding to upgrade the following buildings:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Southern Life Church Moruya</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Broulee Surf Club</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Anglican Parish Batemans Bay (Stage 3)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>SHASA believes it is time to update the strategy to a Community Resilience Strategy and add facilities that need just solar and batteries to reduce their electricity costs.&nbsp; If you know of a community building that may benefit from SHASA’s assistance, please send an email with details to&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:contact.shasa@gmail.com\">contact.shasa@gmail.com</a>&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:open-user-map/map /-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:template-part {\"slug\":\"footer\",\"theme\":\"twentytwentyfive\"} /-->','page-heat-havens','','inherit','closed','closed','','697-revision-v1','','','2025-10-21 13:19:14','2025-10-21 02:19:14','',697,'http://172.19.125.1:8080/?p=854',0,'revision','',0),(856,1,'2025-10-21 13:21:41','2025-10-21 02:21:41','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>SHASA is an incorporated community organisation since February 2015. SHASA’s current Executive has 8 members as approved at our last AGM. Read a little about our current Executive below. Also, see SHASA’s <a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/SHASA-OrgChart2025.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Committee Structure</a> and our <a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/shasa-executive-committee-position-descriptions/\">Executive Committee position descriptions</a>,<br><a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/SHASA-Committee-Structure-2020.pdf\">SHASA Committee-Structure 2020,</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\"}}}} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" style=\"margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"},\"blockGap\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"grid\",\"columnCount\":null,\"minimumColumnWidth\":\"20rem\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"padding-top:0;padding-bottom:0\"><!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">President – Kathryn Maxwell</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Kathryn-1-edited.jpg\",\"id\":804,\"dimRatio\":50,\"overlayColor\":\"contrast\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-804\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Kathryn-1-edited.jpg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\">Kathryn has been a member of SHASA since September 2016 and President for the last 3 years. Kathryn is passionate about achieving a resilient Eurobodalla where we generate more of our electricity and food and keep the money local. Kathryn has extensive project management experience from her work for the Australia and New Zealand Governments in the area of community development and sustainability. A career highlight was her role of Sustainability Manager at the Department of Conservation in New Zealand which included installing the largest off grid solar system and ensuring dozens of conservation islands had solar and energy efficiency upgrades. Kathryn enjoys mountain biking and bushwalking around the region.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Vice President – Andrew Everard</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\",\"id\":291,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f5f7f7\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-291 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f5f7f7\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Treasurer – Patrick Guinness</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/PART_1625626624129.jpg\",\"id\":797,\"dimRatio\":50,\"overlayColor\":\"contrast\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-797 size-full\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/PART_1625626624129.jpg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\">Patrick has worked on community development projects in East Africa, Southeast Asia and Papua New Guinea, including sustainable agriculture, water supply and bio-digester systems, poverty reduction, community organisation, and resettlement programs. Patrick is passionate about tackling climate change and equalising opportunity for the disadvantaged in Australia and overseas . Recently retired from university teaching, Patrick spends his time writing, gardening, bush walking, kayaking, and cycling.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Secretary – Andrea Charlton</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Andrea-Portrait-downscale.jpg\",\"id\":832,\"dimRatio\":50,\"overlayColor\":\"contrast\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-832 size-full\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Andrea-Portrait-downscale.jpg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\">Andrea is a wordsmith and writer who has retired after decades of working for business and government in communication, customer relations and marketing roles. A Canberra resident since 1987, her love affair with the South Coast began with family holidays at Bawley Point, Ulladulla and Guerilla Bay in the late nineties and deepened when her father moved to Batemans Bay in 2010 to be closer to his grandchildren. Her planned retirement move to the Bay was precipitated in 2020 by family needs and her commitment to the region was cemented by the community’s suffering and response to the Black Summer fires. She sees her commitment to SHASA as a way to do something positive to address climate change.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Committee Member – Tony Lowe</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/P1010122-Tony-SHASA-scaled-1-1024x768.jpg\",\"id\":798,\"dimRatio\":50,\"overlayColor\":\"contrast\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-798 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/P1010122-Tony-SHASA-scaled-1-1024x768.jpg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\">Tony has had a love for steam power since growing up near a railway line in the age of steam powered locomotives. He started working life in steam power stations long before they became known as “coal fired”! and went on dealing with that industry and the mining industry specialising in mechanical power transmission. Coal had been a big part of Tony’s career but he realised many years ago that because technologies are now evolving, this has enabled us to leave coal behind. Tony installed his own ground mounted PV Solar system 10 yrs ago and is now very happy to be developing and promoting renewable power solutions in our community.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Committee Member – Lyn Smith</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Lynette-Smith-portrait-2-888x1024.jpg\",\"id\":829,\"dimRatio\":50,\"overlayColor\":\"contrast\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-829 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Lynette-Smith-portrait-2-888x1024.jpg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\">Lyn has been SHASA Facebook administrator and a member of the Communication and Transport Committees since 2022. Lyn moved to the Eurobodalla Shire 41 years ago. She brings a wealth of experience gained over 30 years of teaching and as a Primary School Assistant Principal where she specialised in Environmental Education and School Events. She is enjoying her retirement and volunteering for SHASA, 350Eurobodalla, SECA, Byron Writers Festival and Tennis Australia. Lyn enjoys time spent with family and friends, studying genealogy, attending markets and music festivals, travelling and pottering in her garden.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Committee Member – Matthew Thomas</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\",\"id\":291,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f5f7f7\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-291 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f5f7f7\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Committee Member – Arno Schaaf</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\",\"id\":291,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f5f7f7\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-291 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f5f7f7\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Committee Member – Valerie Faber</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\",\"id\":291,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f5f7f7\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-291 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f5f7f7\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Committee Member – Brett Stevenson</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\",\"id\":291,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f5f7f7\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-291 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f5f7f7\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\">Committee Member – Jo Maclean</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\",\"id\":291,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f5f7f7\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"person-card\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light person-card\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-291 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/woocommerce-placeholder-1024x1024.webp\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f5f7f7\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\"}}}} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" style=\"margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Communications Support Team</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Newsletter Editor</strong> – Kat McCarthy</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Facebook Editor </strong>– Lynette Smith</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Website Administrator</strong> – Natalie Barnett</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>SHASA Sub Committees</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Communications</strong> – Kathryn Maxwell (Chair), Lyn Smith, Andrea Charlton, Natalie Barnett, Linda Leung, Trish Pye, Jo Maclean.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Energy </strong>– Rob Shorrock (Chair), Phil Shorten, Arno Schaaf, Kathryn Maxwell, Tony Lowe, Jude Burger.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Transport (EVs)</strong> – Andrew Everard (Chair), Peter Haughton, Andrea Charlton, Kathryn Maxwell, Arno Schaaf, Matthew Thomas, Natalie Barnett, Tim Herne.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Grants</strong> – Kathryn Maxwell (Chair), Patrick Guinness, Kate Taylor, Andrea Charlton, Arno Schaaf, Stuart Absalom.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Governance</strong> – Kathryn Maxwell (Chair), Pete Phillips, Tony Lowe, Arno Schaaf, Steve Colman, Patrick Guinness, Matthew Thomas.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','People','','inherit','closed','closed','','687-revision-v1','','','2025-10-21 13:21:41','2025-10-21 02:21:41','',687,'http://172.19.125.1:8080/?p=856',0,'revision','',0),(857,1,'2025-10-21 13:24:10','2025-10-21 02:24:10','<!-- wp:template-part {\"slug\":\"header\",\"theme\":\"twentytwentyfive\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.15:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/banner-1024x427.png\",\"id\":163,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#7f93b6\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.17,\"y\":0.51},\"minHeight\":580,\"minHeightUnit\":\"px\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"className\":\"no-margin\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light no-margin\" style=\"min-height:580px\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-163 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.15:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/banner-1024x427.png\" style=\"object-position:17% 51%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"17% 51%\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#7f93b6\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:site-logo {\"width\":219} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1,\"className\":\"is-style-default\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"right\":\"0\",\"left\":\"0\"}}},\"fontSize\":\"xx-large\",\"fontFamily\":\"commissioner\"} -->\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading is-style-default has-commissioner-font-family has-xx-large-font-size\" style=\"padding-right:0;padding-left:0\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-base-color\">Helping Make The </mark><br><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-base-color\">Eurobodalla </mark><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-base-color\">A Better Place To </mark><br><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-base-color\">Live, Work &amp; Play</mark></h1>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button {\"backgroundColor\":\"accent-2\",\"textColor\":\"accent-1\",\"style\":{\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"var:preset|color|accent-1\"}}},\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\",\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\",\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\"}}}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-accent-1-color has-accent-2-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-element-button\" href=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/?page_id=590\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)\">Donate Now</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|30\",\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|30\",\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\",\"justifyContent\":\"center\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\"><!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"66.66%\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\"><!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"dimensions\":{\"minHeight\":\"376px\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"min-height:376px\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">Southcoast Health &amp; Sustainability Alliance</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Community-led solutions including</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Proactive responses to the&nbsp;climate crisis&nbsp;including drought, floods and bushfires</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Community&nbsp;solar and energy efficiency projects</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Community engagement, local food &amp; water security</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">The municipality of Eurobodalla covers 110km of the south coast between Durras and Wallaga Lake including Bateman’s Bay, Mogo, Moruya, Tuross Head, Narooma and many hamlets in between. With our recent experiences of drought, bushfires, floods and COVID 19, Eurobodalla has a great opportunity to<strong>&nbsp;reinvent</strong>&nbsp;itself.&nbsp;<strong>New technologies, new thinking, new living and new work opportunities</strong>&nbsp;can help us create an inspiring future for all as we move to a better, cleaner economy.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Check out our strategic plan&nbsp;<a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/SHASA2030-1124s.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SHASA’s 2030 Vision</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Our Aim:&nbsp;<strong>100% Renewable Energy Eurobodalla by 2030</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Acknowledgement of Country –&nbsp;<em>SHASA recognises Aboriginal people of the Yuin Nation as the original inhabitants and custodians of all land and water in the Eurobodalla and respects their enduring cultural and spiritual connection to it. SHASA acknowledges the Traditional Owners of the land in which we live and we pay our respect to Elders past, present and emerging.</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"33.33%\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\"><!-- wp:group {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\",\"left\":\"0\",\"right\":\"0\"},\"margin\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"}},\"dimensions\":{\"minHeight\":\"0px\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"min-height:0px;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-top:0;padding-right:0;padding-bottom:0;padding-left:0\"><!-- wp:heading {\"style\":{\"layout\":{\"selfStretch\":\"fit\",\"flexSize\":null}}} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Recent News</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:rss {\"feedURL\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis/rss\",\"itemsToShow\":4,\"displayAuthor\":true,\"displayDate\":true,\"className\":\"rss-feed\",\"style\":{\"layout\":{\"selfStretch\":\"fit\",\"flexSize\":null},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"var:preset|color|accent-3\"}}}},\"textColor\":\"contrast\"} /--></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"className\":\"is-style-default\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"right\":\"0\",\"left\":\"0\"}}}} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-left is-style-default\" style=\"margin-right:0;margin-left:0\">Community Led Solutions</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:shortcode -->\n[ymc_filter id=\"800\"]\n<!-- /wp:shortcode -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"className\":\"is-style-default\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"right\":\"0\",\"left\":\"0\"}}}} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading is-style-default\" style=\"margin-right:0;margin-left:0\">Community Events</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:shortcode -->\n[em_events view=\"listweek\" disable_filter=\"0\" filter_elements=\"date_range\"]\n<!-- /wp:shortcode --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"is-style-default\",\"style\":{\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"var:preset|color|base\"}}},\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|30\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|30\"}}},\"backgroundColor\":\"accent-1\",\"textColor\":\"base\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"flexWrap\":\"nowrap\",\"justifyContent\":\"center\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-style-default has-base-color has-accent-1-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color\" style=\"padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Support sustainability in our community</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button {\"backgroundColor\":\"accent-2\",\"textColor\":\"accent-1\",\"style\":{\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"var:preset|color|accent-1\"}}},\"border\":{\"radius\":\"100px\",\"width\":\"0px\",\"style\":\"none\"},\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\",\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|40\",\"top\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\",\"bottom\":\"var:preset|spacing|20\"}}},\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-accent-1-color has-accent-2-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color has-medium-font-size has-custom-font-size wp-element-button\" href=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/?page_id=590\" style=\"border-style:none;border-width:0px;border-radius:100px;padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--40)\">Donate Now</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaPosition\":\"right\",\"mediaId\":455,\"mediaLink\":\"http://172.19.125.111:8080/?attachment_id=455\",\"mediaType\":\"image\",\"mediaWidth\":25,\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|60\",\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|60\"}}}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile\" style=\"padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);grid-template-columns:auto 25%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:wpforms/form-selector {\"clientId\":\"a126e1b4-e03e-4c76-b9f1-a0d7f75c8d27\",\"formId\":\"440\",\"displayTitle\":true,\"theme\":\"default\",\"themeName\":\"Default\",\"copyPasteJsonValue\":\"{\\u0022displayTitle\\u0022:true,\\u0022displayDesc\\u0022:false,\\u0022theme\\u0022:\\u0022default\\u0022,\\u0022themeName\\u0022:\\u0022Default\\u0022,\\u0022fieldSize\\u0022:\\u0022medium\\u0022,\\u0022backgroundImage\\u0022:\\u0022none\\u0022,\\u0022backgroundPosition\\u0022:\\u0022center center\\u0022,\\u0022backgroundRepeat\\u0022:\\u0022no-repeat\\u0022,\\u0022backgroundSizeMode\\u0022:\\u0022cover\\u0022,\\u0022backgroundSize\\u0022:\\u0022cover\\u0022,\\u0022backgroundWidth\\u0022:\\u0022100px\\u0022,\\u0022backgroundHeight\\u0022:\\u0022100px\\u0022,\\u0022backgroundUrl\\u0022:\\u0022url()\\u0022,\\u0022backgroundColor\\u0022:\\u0022rgba( 0, 0, 0, 0 )\\u0022,\\u0022fieldBorderRadius\\u0022:\\u00223px\\u0022,\\u0022fieldBorderStyle\\u0022:\\u0022solid\\u0022,\\u0022fieldBorderSize\\u0022:\\u00221px\\u0022,\\u0022fieldBackgroundColor\\u0022:\\u0022#ffffff\\u0022,\\u0022fieldBorderColor\\u0022:\\u0022rgba( 0, 0, 0, 0.25 )\\u0022,\\u0022fieldTextColor\\u0022:\\u0022rgba( 0, 0, 0, 0.7 )\\u0022,\\u0022fieldMenuColor\\u0022:\\u0022#ffffff\\u0022,\\u0022labelSize\\u0022:\\u0022medium\\u0022,\\u0022labelColor\\u0022:\\u0022rgba( 0, 0, 0, 0.85 )\\u0022,\\u0022labelSublabelColor\\u0022:\\u0022rgba( 0, 0, 0, 0.55 )\\u0022,\\u0022labelErrorColor\\u0022:\\u0022#d63637\\u0022,\\u0022buttonSize\\u0022:\\u0022medium\\u0022,\\u0022buttonBorderStyle\\u0022:\\u0022none\\u0022,\\u0022buttonBorderSize\\u0022:\\u00221px\\u0022,\\u0022buttonBorderRadius\\u0022:\\u00223px\\u0022,\\u0022buttonBackgroundColor\\u0022:\\u0022#066aab\\u0022,\\u0022buttonTextColor\\u0022:\\u0022#ffffff\\u0022,\\u0022buttonBorderColor\\u0022:\\u0022#066aab\\u0022,\\u0022pageBreakColor\\u0022:\\u0022#066aab\\u0022,\\u0022containerPadding\\u0022:\\u00220px\\u0022,\\u0022containerBorderStyle\\u0022:\\u0022none\\u0022,\\u0022containerBorderWidth\\u0022:\\u00221px\\u0022,\\u0022containerBorderColor\\u0022:\\u0022#000000\\u0022,\\u0022containerBorderRadius\\u0022:\\u00223px\\u0022,\\u0022containerShadowSize\\u0022:\\u0022none\\u0022,\\u0022customCss\\u0022:\\u0022\\u0022}\"} /--></div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"http://172.19.125.111:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/priscilla-du-preez-XkKCui44iM0-unsplash.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-455 size-full\"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:template-part {\"slug\":\"footer\",\"theme\":\"twentytwentyfive\"} /-->','Front Page','Displays your site\'s home page, whether it is set to display latest posts or a static page. The Front Page template takes precedence over all templates.','inherit','closed','closed','','510-revision-v1','','','2025-10-21 13:24:10','2025-10-21 02:24:10','',510,'http://172.19.125.1:8080/?p=857',0,'revision','',0),(859,1,'2025-10-21 13:44:36','2025-10-21 02:44:36','<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">What Is SHASA</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\">In 2014 a walk was held in Moruya to highlight climate change. A small group of interested local community members who attended this walk, then formed a group to undertake projects to help achieve a zero carbon Eurobodalla. This group was named Southcoast Health and Sustainability Alliance (SHASA) and was incorporated on the 29th February 2016. SHASA has an Executive of 8 members.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Other community members attend the meetings to participate in projects across the Eurobodalla. All community members are welcomed resulting in a busy group of people attending monthly meetings (held via Zoom) and implementing practical solutions to build community leadership, resilience, and capability to deal with our climate chaos and it’s many impacts including drought, flood, and bushfire.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"50px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"metadata\":{\"name\":\"Featured Category Triple\",\"categories\":[\"featured-selling\"],\"patternName\":\"woocommerce-blocks/featured-category-triple\"},\"align\":\"wide\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"calc( 0.5 * var(\\u002d\\u002dwp\\u002d\\u002dstyle\\u002d\\u002droot\\u002d\\u002dpadding-right, var(\\u002d\\u002dwp\\u002d\\u002dcustom\\u002d\\u002dgap\\u002d\\u002dhorizontal)))\",\"bottom\":\"0\",\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\",\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\"},\"margin\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\",\"justifyContent\":\"center\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignwide\" style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-top:calc( 0.5 * var(--wp--style--root--padding-right, var(--wp--custom--gap--horizontal)));padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);padding-bottom:0;padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)\"><!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column {\"className\":\"is-style-default\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-style-default\"><!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=687\">People &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=689\">Achievements &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=786\">Governance &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"justifyContent\":\"left\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=683\">Get Involved &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">More</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA have recently updated our <a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/SHASA2030-1124s.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">strategic plan</a> to 2030. It outlines our key areas of focus for the next decade and will be regularly reviewed. All feedback welcomed via our <a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/contact/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">contact page</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">SHASA’s Business Partnerships</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Moruya Bicycles</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA has offered a solar panel bulk buy program to its members since 2017. Initially, several contractors were engaged to supply and install the panels. After the first round, it was clear that MESA customers reported the highest satisfaction with installation and after-sales support. MESA is now SHASA’s exclusive supplier for Solar systems, battery storage and EV chargers under the ongoing Eurobodalla Community Solar program. They also provide competitive quotes and installation services for community organisations.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Together, SHASA and MESA have installed over 450 roof top solar systems, to the Eurobodalla. For each installation up to 6.6 kW, MESA makes a contribution to SHASA’s community work.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">They have also worked together to deliver many community projects including SHASA’s Heatwave and Bushfire Refuge program, Community Solar Installations, the Moos Bushfire recovery Newsletter, voluntary RFS upgrades to facilities, the Microgrid Feasibility Study, and the Power on the Move mobile generator, for use by the community.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">MESA provides SHASA with technical advice, training and consultation on Renewable Energy and general electrical technology and practices.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA places a high value on the expertise, diligence and integrity that MESA brings to all business carried out for SHASA.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Moruya Bicycles</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA entered into a partnership with Moruya Bicycles in 2018 to run an E-bike hire service in Moruya. SHASA purchased two electric all road bikes and Moruya Bicycles operates the E-Bike hire at no cost to SHASA.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">The bikes are upgraded regularly to facilitate the sale of second hand E-bikes in Moruya.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Moruya Bicycles operates the hire service at no profit to themselves, all money from the hire fees goes towards the cost of maintaining and upgrading the E-Bikes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->','About Us','','inherit','closed','closed','','154-revision-v1','','','2025-10-21 13:44:36','2025-10-21 02:44:36','',154,'http://172.19.125.1:8080/?p=859',0,'revision','',0),(860,1,'2025-10-21 13:45:05','2025-10-21 02:45:05','<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">What Is SHASA</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\">In 2014 a walk was held in Moruya to highlight climate change. A small group of interested local community members who attended this walk, then formed a group to undertake projects to help achieve a zero carbon Eurobodalla. This group was named Southcoast Health and Sustainability Alliance (SHASA) and was incorporated on the 29th February 2016. SHASA has an Executive of 8 members.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Other community members attend the meetings to participate in projects across the Eurobodalla. All community members are welcomed resulting in a busy group of people attending monthly meetings (held via Zoom) and implementing practical solutions to build community leadership, resilience, and capability to deal with our climate chaos and it’s many impacts including drought, flood, and bushfire.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"50px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"metadata\":{\"name\":\"Featured Category Triple\",\"categories\":[\"featured-selling\"],\"patternName\":\"woocommerce-blocks/featured-category-triple\"},\"align\":\"wide\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"calc( 0.5 * var(\\u002d\\u002dwp\\u002d\\u002dstyle\\u002d\\u002droot\\u002d\\u002dpadding-right, var(\\u002d\\u002dwp\\u002d\\u002dcustom\\u002d\\u002dgap\\u002d\\u002dhorizontal)))\",\"bottom\":\"0\",\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\",\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\"},\"margin\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\",\"justifyContent\":\"center\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignwide\" style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-top:calc( 0.5 * var(--wp--style--root--padding-right, var(--wp--custom--gap--horizontal)));padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);padding-bottom:0;padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)\"><!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column {\"className\":\"is-style-default\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-style-default\"><!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=687\">People &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=689\">Achievements &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=786\">Governance &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"justifyContent\":\"left\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=683\">Get Involved &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">More</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA have recently updated our <a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/SHASA2030-1124s.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">strategic plan</a> to 2030. It outlines our key areas of focus for the next decade and will be regularly reviewed. All feedback welcomed via our <a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/contact/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">contact page</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">SHASA’s Business Partnerships</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Moruya Bicycles</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA has offered a solar panel bulk buy program to its members since 2017. Initially, several contractors were engaged to supply and install the panels. After the first round, it was clear that MESA customers reported the highest satisfaction with installation and after-sales support. MESA is now SHASA’s exclusive supplier for Solar systems, battery storage and EV chargers under the ongoing Eurobodalla Community Solar program. They also provide competitive quotes and installation services for community organisations.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Together, SHASA and MESA have installed over 450 roof top solar systems, to the Eurobodalla. For each installation up to 6.6 kW, MESA makes a contribution to SHASA’s community work.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">They have also worked together to deliver many community projects including SHASA’s Heatwave and Bushfire Refuge program, Community Solar Installations, the Moos Bushfire recovery Newsletter, voluntary RFS upgrades to facilities, the Microgrid Feasibility Study, and the Power on the Move mobile generator, for use by the community.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">MESA provides SHASA with technical advice, training and consultation on Renewable Energy and general electrical technology and practices.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA places a high value on the expertise, diligence and integrity that MESA brings to all business carried out for SHASA.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Moruya Bicycles</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA entered into a partnership with Moruya Bicycles in 2018 to run an E-bike hire service in Moruya. SHASA purchased two electric all road bikes and Moruya Bicycles operates the E-Bike hire at no cost to SHASA.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">The bikes are upgraded regularly to facilitate the sale of second hand E-bikes in Moruya.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Moruya Bicycles operates the hire service at no profit to themselves, all money from the hire fees goes towards the cost of maintaining and upgrading the E-Bikes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->','About Us','','inherit','closed','closed','','154-revision-v1','','','2025-10-21 13:45:05','2025-10-21 02:45:05','',154,'http://172.19.125.1:8080/?p=860',0,'revision','',0),(861,1,'2025-10-21 13:45:33','2025-10-21 02:45:33','<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">What Is SHASA</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\">In 2014 a walk was held in Moruya to highlight climate change. A small group of interested local community members who attended this walk, then formed a group to undertake projects to help achieve a zero carbon Eurobodalla. This group was named Southcoast Health and Sustainability Alliance (SHASA) and was incorporated on the 29th February 2016. SHASA has an Executive of 8 members.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Other community members attend the meetings to participate in projects across the Eurobodalla. All community members are welcomed resulting in a busy group of people attending monthly meetings (held via Zoom) and implementing practical solutions to build community leadership, resilience, and capability to deal with our climate chaos and it’s many impacts including drought, flood, and bushfire.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"50px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"metadata\":{\"name\":\"Featured Category Triple\",\"categories\":[\"featured-selling\"],\"patternName\":\"woocommerce-blocks/featured-category-triple\"},\"align\":\"wide\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"calc( 0.5 * var(\\u002d\\u002dwp\\u002d\\u002dstyle\\u002d\\u002droot\\u002d\\u002dpadding-right, var(\\u002d\\u002dwp\\u002d\\u002dcustom\\u002d\\u002dgap\\u002d\\u002dhorizontal)))\",\"bottom\":\"0\",\"left\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\",\"right\":\"var:preset|spacing|50\"},\"margin\":{\"top\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\"}}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\",\"justifyContent\":\"center\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignwide\" style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;padding-top:calc( 0.5 * var(--wp--style--root--padding-right, var(--wp--custom--gap--horizontal)));padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50);padding-bottom:0;padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)\"><!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column {\"className\":\"is-style-default\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-style-default\"><!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#d8d6d6\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278 size-full\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#d8d6d6\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=687\">People &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#d8d6d6\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278 size-full\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#d8d6d6\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=689\">Achievements &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#d8d6d6\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278 size-full\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#d8d6d6\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=786\">Governance &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\",\"id\":278,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#d8d6d6\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":false,\"contentPosition\":\"bottom left\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"style\":{\"color\":[]}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-278 size-full\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://172.19.125.1:8080/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/2-4.jpeg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#d8d6d6\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:buttons {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"justifyContent\":\"left\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/?page_id=683\">Get Involved &gt;</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">More</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA have recently updated our <a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/SHASA2030-1124s.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">strategic plan</a> to 2030. It outlines our key areas of focus for the next decade and will be regularly reviewed. All feedback welcomed via our <a href=\"https://shasa.com.au/contact/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">contact page</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">SHASA’s Business Partnerships</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Moruya Bicycles</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA has offered a solar panel bulk buy program to its members since 2017. Initially, several contractors were engaged to supply and install the panels. After the first round, it was clear that MESA customers reported the highest satisfaction with installation and after-sales support. MESA is now SHASA’s exclusive supplier for Solar systems, battery storage and EV chargers under the ongoing Eurobodalla Community Solar program. They also provide competitive quotes and installation services for community organisations.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Together, SHASA and MESA have installed over 450 roof top solar systems, to the Eurobodalla. For each installation up to 6.6 kW, MESA makes a contribution to SHASA’s community work.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">They have also worked together to deliver many community projects including SHASA’s Heatwave and Bushfire Refuge program, Community Solar Installations, the Moos Bushfire recovery Newsletter, voluntary RFS upgrades to facilities, the Microgrid Feasibility Study, and the Power on the Move mobile generator, for use by the community.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">MESA provides SHASA with technical advice, training and consultation on Renewable Energy and general electrical technology and practices.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA places a high value on the expertise, diligence and integrity that MESA brings to all business carried out for SHASA.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Moruya Bicycles</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">SHASA entered into a partnership with Moruya Bicycles in 2018 to run an E-bike hire service in Moruya. SHASA purchased two electric all road bikes and Moruya Bicycles operates the E-Bike hire at no cost to SHASA.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">The bikes are upgraded regularly to facilitate the sale of second hand E-bikes in Moruya.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Moruya Bicycles operates the hire service at no profit to themselves, all money from the hire fees goes towards the cost of maintaining and upgrading the E-Bikes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->','About Us','','inherit','closed','closed','','154-revision-v1','','','2025-10-21 13:45:33','2025-10-21 02:45:33','',154,'http://172.19.125.1:8080/?p=861',0,'revision','',0),(863,1,'2025-10-21 13:45:42','2025-10-21 02:45:42','<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"flex\",\"orientation\":\"vertical\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-accent-1-color\">What Is SHASA</mark></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left has-medium-font-size\">In 2014 a walk was held in Moruya to highlight climate change. A small group of interested local community members who attended this walk, then formed a group to undertake projects to help achieve a zero carbon Eurobodalla. This group was named Southcoast Health and Sustainability Alliance (SHASA) and was incorporated on the 29th February 2016. SHASA has an Executive of 8 members.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"medium\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Other community members attend the meetings to participate in projects across the Eurobodalla. All community members are welcomed resulting in a busy group of people attending monthly meetings (held via Zoom) and implementing practical solutions to build community leadership, resilience, and capability to deal with our climate chaos and it’s many impacts including drought, flood, and bushfire.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"50px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- w